* ''The wards bind the daemon and kahua wikis; user wikis keep full caps'' (operator: //"We do want users to have full caps over their wikis, but the daemon/kahua wiki should get bound by these wards."//). A user's own wiki keeps promote, kāpae and lift advisory, and the AI drives every act beside the operator there. The daemon wiki and the kahua stage bind their code-bearing acts, StartupActions included: a StartupAction there runs from genesis or the promoted set alone, and its promotion rides the ward. Bound acts: `promote-commit`, `kapae-lower`, item 7's house cap and push lei. Free acts: `kapae-raise`, `promote-drop`, `orphan-drop` and `promote-keep`; a kahua lift rides the ward since 2026-11-05 (#/rulings). Item 7 builds the ward and the founding waits on item 7; PR #157 carries no interim refusal. The `lift.capability-tension` loop closes for daemon and kahua when the ward lands and stays open for user wikis.

